.description = "frontmatter, sections and rss in .smd files",
---

pages are [SuperMD](https://zine-ssg.io/docs/supermd/) (`.smd`) - markdown with a
ziggy frontmatter block:

```zig
---
.title = "My page",
.date = .date("2026-08-23T10:00:00"),
.description = "Shown in listings and OG images",
.layout = "page.shtml",
.tags = ["diary"],
---
```

# sections

a directory with an `index.smd` becomes a section. section indexes use
`layout = "section.shtml"` and can attach feeds:

```zig
.alternatives = [
    .{
        .name = "rss",
        .layout = "rss.xml",
        .output = "index.xml",
        .type = "application/rss+xml",
    },
],
```

that renders `index.xml` next to the section - exactly how the
`/updates/` feed on this site works. with `features.rss` on, each feed
also gets a discovery `<link>` in `<head>`.

# translations

mirrored pages live under matching paths in each locale dir
(`content/en/foo.smd` <-> `content/ru/foo.smd`), the language switcher
pairs them automatically. ui strings come from `i18n/<locale>.json`.
pages missing a translation get a small notice banner unless you turn
`translation_notice` off.

# tips

- `.tags` powers the `/tags/` index, any string works, spaces become
  dashes in urls
- reading time and word count are computed automatically for recents
- dates drive ordering everywhere: recents widgets, prev/next, feeds
